PART C -- HYP-8315: the extremals, pushed to n = 8 (where NO regular T exists)
==============================================================================
  n  transitive = (n-1)!      MIN found  min = transitive?        MAX found                 max scores
  4                    6              6               True               10               [1, 1, 2, 2]
  5                   24             24               True               55            [2, 2, 2, 2, 2]
  6                  120            120               True              333         [2, 2, 2, 3, 3, 3]
  7                  720            720               True             2744      [3, 3, 3, 3, 3, 3, 3]
  8                 5040           5040               True            23363   [3, 3, 3, 3, 4, 4, 4, 4]
  n <= 6 rows are EXHAUSTIVE; n = 7,8 are hill-climbing (60 restarts) so the MAX is
  a lower bound, not certified.  The MIN is compared against the transitive value.
  At EVEN n there is no regular tournament, so 'Paley maximises' does not even parse
  -- read off what the maximiser's score sequence actually is.

==============================================================================
PART D -- HYP-8390c: the 2-adic law for sum_r a_r under ordinal sum
==============================================================================
  Sa(T1 (+) T2) = Sa(T1) * det(p I + L_in(T2)),  so  v2 is ADDITIVE:
      v2(Sa(T1(+)T2)) = v2(Sa(T1)) + v2( det(p I + L_in(T2)) ).
  For the transitive tower TT_n = TT_{n-1} (+) . the shift is exactly p = n-1, so
      v2(Sa(TT_n)) = v2((n-1)!) = (n-1) - s_2(n-1)   (Legendre).

  n  Sa(TT_n)=(n-1)!   v2   Legendre (n-1)-s2(n-1)    ok
  3                2    1                        1  True
  4                6    1                        1  True
  5               24    3                        3  True
  6              120    3                        3  True
  7              720    4                        4  True
  8             5040    4                        4  True
  9            40320    7                        7  True
 10           362880    7                        7  True
 11          3628800    8                        8  True

  And the general law is just additivity of v2 over the ordinal-sum factorisation --
  no special 2-adic structure beyond Legendre on the size factors.  So HYP-8390c has
  a clean answer and it is not deep: v2 is additive because Sa is multiplicative
  ALONG THE TOWER, with the shift supplying the only new 2-content.
